---
import Component from "../../../src/components/donate/GoalMeter.astro";
import "../../../src/styles/tokens.css";

// Isolation page for GoalMeter — codeyam screenshots the #codeyam-capture wrapper
// by navigating to /isolated-components/GoalMeter.
//
// READ THE CAPTURE CAREFULLY, because this page overrides the component's own
// behaviour to produce one.
//
// The band ships hidden and reveals itself only once Givebutter's loader script
// has defined `<givebutter-widget>`. Neither thing happens here: the loader is
// not on this page, and the capture browser does not run the reveal even when it
// is (confirmed empirically — a JS-driven reveal that works in a live browser
// still captures blank). So on a real page inside a capture, this band collapses
// to nothing, which is the DESIGNED behaviour and not a fault.
//
// The style block below therefore forces the band visible, so the frame we own —
// the paper-2 band, the heading, the reserved meter area, the section rhythm —
// can be seen and reviewed at all. What this frame proves is that layout. What
// it does NOT prove is that the meter renders: the empty area under the heading
// is exactly the boundary between our band and Givebutter's progress bar, and no
// screenshot taken here can show their side of it.
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Isolated: GoalMeter</title>
    <style is:global>
      /* Harness-only. Defeats the component's collapse so the band is
         reviewable; see the note above for what that does and does not show.
         `is:global` because the band is rendered by the imported component and
         so carries ITS scope id, not this page's — a scoped rule here would be
         rewritten to a selector that matches nothing. */
      #codeyam-capture .goal-meter.is-collapsed {
        display: block;
      }
      /* The capture wrapper is fit-content, and this band's only intrinsic
         width is its heading — the meter area is empty here because Givebutter
         draws nothing on this page. Pin a page-like width so the band is
         reviewed at the proportions it actually has on /donate. */
      #codeyam-capture {
        width: 1200px;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div id="codeyam-capture">
      <Component title="Our progress" widgetId="MRDbEz" />
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
